language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Schedule the jobs, each with a duration and resource needs, so that precedence constraints hold, the use of every resource stays within its capacity at all times, and the makespan is minimised.
given durations_data_dim1 : int(1..)
given durations_data : matrix indexed by [int(1..durations_data_dim1)] of int(0..)
given resource_needs_data_dim1, resource_needs_data_dim2 : int(1..)
given resource_needs_data : matrix indexed by [int(1..resource_needs_data_dim1), int(1..resource_needs_data_dim2)] of int(0..)
given resource_capacities_data_dim1 : int(1..)
given resource_capacities_data : matrix indexed by [int(1..resource_capacities_data_dim1)] of int(0..)
$ successors_link_data[e,1] precedes successors_link_data[e,2] (jobs are numbered from 0 in the data)
given successors_link_data_dim1, successors_link_data_dim2 : int(1..)
given successors_link_data : matrix indexed by [int(1..successors_link_data_dim1), int(1..successors_link_data_dim2)] of int(0..)
$ start_time[j] is the start time of job j (job j+1 in model numbering)
find start_time : matrix indexed by [int(1..durations_data_dim1)] of int(0..sum(durations_data))
find makespan : int(0..sum(durations_data))

branching on [start_time]
heuristic conflict

minimising makespan
such that
$ the project makespan is at least the finish time of every job
forAll j : int(1..durations_data_dim1) . makespan >= start_time[j] + durations_data[j],
$ a job starts only after each of its predecessors has finished
forAll e : int(1..successors_link_data_dim1) . (start_time[successors_link_data[e,1]+1] + durations_data[successors_link_data[e,1]+1] <= start_time[successors_link_data[e,2]+1]),
$ at every time the total need of a resource by the running jobs stays within the capacity of that resource
forAll r : int(1..resource_capacities_data_dim1) . cumulative(start_time, durations_data, resource_needs_data[..,r], resource_capacities_data[r])
